        "body": "## \u26a0\ufe0f Exploration by an LLM\n\n> **Note:** This is an exploratory draft PR generated by an LLM (opencode) to investigate [issue #6008](https://github.com/homarr-labs/homarr/issues/6008). It is **not** ready for merge \u2014 please review critically for correctness and conventions before considering.\n\n## Problem\n\n`/manage/about` fails entirely with `ECONNREFUSED` and renders the default Next.js full-page error (`digest: 3227098399`), leaving the page unusable.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`apps/nextjs/src/app/[locale]/manage/about/page.tsx` fetched its **own** API routes over HTTP:\n\n```ts\nconst baseServerUrl = `http://${await getHostAsync()}`; // http://$HOSTNAME:3000\nconst dependencies = await fetch(`${baseServerUrl}/api/about/dependencies`)...\nconst githubContributors = await fetch(`${baseServerUrl}/api/about/contributors/github`)...\n// ...crowdin, opencollective\n```\n\nWhen the Next.js server cannot reach itself (`HOSTNAME` misconfigured, restricted container networking, reverse-proxy where the app cannot loop back to `localhost:3000`), every `fetch()` throws `ECONNREFUSED`, and with **no `error.tsx`** anywhere except two tool pages, the error bubbles to the root and shows the ugly default error page.\n\nWorse: all four `/api/about/*` routes are `force-static` \u2014 three just serve static JSON files and one calls `getDependenciesAsync()` directly. The HTTP round-trip is entirely unnecessary.\n\n## Changes (3 files, +52/-29)\n\n1. **`manage/about/page.tsx`** \u2014 Removed the 4 `fetch()` calls and `getHostAsync()`. Import the static JSON files directly (already imported as types) and call `getDependenciesAsync()` directly. This eliminates the self-network dependency entirely, fixing the ECONNREFUSED root cause *and* removing a pointless round-trip.\n\n2. **`manage/error.tsx`** (new) \u2014 A manage-level error boundary (Next.js 16 `error.tsx` convention) using the `unstable_retry` prop. Any future runtime error in a manage page renders a friendly, localised fallback **inside the existing manage layout** (sidebar stays usable) instead of the default full-page error.\n\n3. **`lang/en.json`** \u2014 Added `management.error.{title,text,digest}` translation keys (other locales fall back to `en` via the existing deepmerge mechanism, keeping the diff minimal).\n\n## Why this approach\n\n- **Fixes the cause, not just the symptom** \u2014 the crash cannot happen anymore because there is no self-fetch.\n- **Defense in depth** \u2014 the error boundary catches *any* future runtime error across all `/manage/*` pages while preserving navigation.\n- **Minimal** \u2014 uses Context7 to verify the latest Next.js 16.2.9 error-handling API; follows the existing `manage/tools/{docker,kubernetes}/error.tsx` pattern.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsc --noEmit` passes on the nextjs app.\n- `oxlint` clean (only pre-existing warnings in untouched code).\n- `en.json` validates as JSON.\n\nNot yet runtime-tested; reviewer should verify `/manage/about` loads and that an error in a manage sub-page shows the boundary.\n\nRefs #6008",
